  "articleBody": "Turning a garage into a livable room can go off track quickly if key details get skipped during planning. Here are frequent missteps to avoid.\n\n1. Skipping required permits. Don't start framing before building, electrical, and mechanical permits are issued; work done without sign-offs can face costly tear-outs.\n2. Ignoring moisture barriers on the concrete slab. Standard garage slabs lack sub-slab vapor retarders, so laying finished flooring directly on concrete invites dampness. Install an approved barrier first.\n3. Sealing the garage door infill poorly. Framing the exterior opening without treated bottom plates or proper flashing leads to rot and water intrusion.\n4. Covering rough-in work prematurely. Putting up insulation and drywall before inspectors approve wiring and framing fails code compliance.\n5. Forgetting heating, cooling, and ventilation needs. A space meant for living must maintain comfort without overburdening your primary HVAC system.\n\nCommon Mistakes to Avoid: The costliest error is rushing into finishes before verifying site conditions and plan approvals. \n\nFor hands-on project coordination and solid finish work, reach out to HH Remodeling LLC at 303-505-0866.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-23"
